<title>KUWAIT: Kuwait bank assets rise 0.2 pct in July.</title>
<headline>Kuwait bank assets rise 0.2 pct in July.</headline>
<dateline>KUWAIT 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Combined assets of Kuwaiti banks rose 0.2 percent to 11.220 billion dinars at the end of July from 11.194 billion at the end of June, the Central Bank's monthly bulletin said.</p>
<p>Assets were 11.300 billion dinars in July 1995.</p>
<p>			 Figures in million Kuwaiti dinars</p>
<p>					     July '96	  July '95</p>
<p> Cash					  43.7		 47.4</p>
<p> Balances with Central Bank	     7.8		 22.2</p>
<p> Public debt instruments	     1876.4	     2020.5</p>
<p> Debt purchase bonds		   3132.4	     3728.4</p>
<p> Other					 --		    0.2</p>
<p> Other local investments		306.0		283.9</p>
<p>Credit facilities to</p>
<p>  residents				2814.0	     2112.0</p>
<p> Foreign assets			  2079.4	     1938.2</p>
<p> Inter bank local deposits	    475.0		663.3</p>
<p> Other assets			     485.4		484.0</p>
<p> Total				    11220.1	    11300.1</p>
<p>Note - Data covers eight commercial and specialised banks, the Islamic institution Kuwait Finance House and a Kuwaiti branch of a Bahrain-based bank.</p>
<p>Debt purchase bonds include the value of the purchase by the government of the real estate portfolio of Kuwait Finance House in December 1991.</p>
<p>Slight discrepancies in totals are due to rounding.</p>
<p>($1 = 0.299 dinars)</p>
<p>-- Inal Ersan, Kuwait newsroom +965-243-1920</p>
